The **[[obj:parotidduct]]** leaves the anterior edge of the **[[obj:parotidgland]]** midway between the zygomatic arch and the corner of the mouth [1].

It then:

- crosses the face in a transverse direction [1];
- crosses the medial border of the masseter muscle [1];
- turns deeply into the buccal fat pad and pierces the buccinator muscle [1];
- opens into the oral cavity near the second upper molar tooth [1].

A related description states that it passes anteriorly across the external surface of the masseter muscle, turns medially to penetrate the buccinator muscle, and opens adjacent to the crown of the second upper molar tooth [3].
